<TextPage
	title="About — Hookd"
	description="A personal crochet blog: patterns written out in full, and write-ups of yarn, fibre and stitch tests. Not a shop."
	heading="About"
	standfirst="Crochet patterns, and write-ups of the tests behind them."
	active="about"
>
	<p>
		I design crochet patterns and test the yarn that goes into them. The testing happened
		privately for years — swatches, wash tests, gauge measured twice and written on a scrap of
		paper that went in a drawer. This site is where that stops being private.
	</p>

	<h2>What is here</h2>

	<p>
		<strong>Patterns</strong>, written out in full. No video-only instructions, and nothing
		left to guess. Sizes and gauge are
		stated the way the Craft Yarn Council defines them, and gauge is measured on the actual
		piece after blocking — not on a swatch pinned flat, because those two numbers differ and
		almost no published pattern admits it.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>The journal</strong> is the working-out: yarn tests, stitch tests, fibre notes.
		Everything gets swatched, washed and measured before it gets written about, including the
		results that were inconvenient.
	</p>

	<h2>What is not here</h2>

	<p>
		This is not a shop. There are no carts, no accounts, no newsletter pop-up over the
		recipe. Anything I sell lives on Ravelry, never here.
	</p>

	<h2>Using the patterns</h2>

	<p>
		Make them, gift them, and sell what you make. The <a href="/licence/">pattern terms</a> set
		that out properly, but that is the short version.
	</p>
</TextPage>
